+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+Native Windows ARM64 (`aarch64`) support for xz 5.8.4 as shipped in the MSYS2
+`usr/bin` layer of Git for Windows, on branch `arm64-port`.
+
+The target is **aarch64-pc-cygwin**: binaries link against the ARM64
+MSYS2 runtime (`msys-2.0.dll`) and are named like the x86_64 MSYS2 package
+(`xz.exe`, `msys-lzma-5.dll`, ...). It is not an MSVC build. xz upstream does
+not ship an MSVC project, and the Git for Windows `usr/bin` layer is built
+against the MSYS2 runtime.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- None. The checked-in autotools build already handles `--host=aarch64-pc-cygwin`:
+  - `build-aux/config.sub` accepts the triplet.
+  - MSYS2's libtool names the DLL `msys-lzma-5.dll`.
+  - The x86 asm (`COND_ASM_X86`) and CLMUL checks are disabled because of the host.
+  - The prefixed `objdump` and `windres` are picked up, so `.rc` resources are built for ARM64 and the unaligned-access probe answers `yes`.
+
+### Source Code
+- `src/liblzma/check/crc_common.h`: the ARM64 CRC32 runtime-detection selector now also accepts `__CYGWIN__` (commit `e18e5ff`).
+- `src/liblzma/check/crc32_arm64.h`: on `__CYGWIN__`, includes `<windows.h>` and detects the instructions with `IsProcessorFeaturePresent(PF_ARM_V8_CRC32_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE)` (commit `e18e5ff`).
+- Reason for both changes: Cygwin/MSYS2 GCC defines neither `_WIN32` nor `__ARM_FEATURE_CRC32`, and it has no `getauxval`. As a result `CRC_ARM64_RUNTIME_DETECTION` was never defined, and liblzma silently compiled out its ARM64 CRC32 code. It then used the generic table CRC, even though configure reported "ARM64 CRC32 instruction is usable... yes".
+
+### CI/CD
+- None. This checkout has no CI configuration.
+
+### New Files
+- `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`, `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`: ARM64 benchmark results.
+- `ARM64-PORT.md`: this document.
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites:
+- MSYS2 with the aarch64-pc-cygwin cross toolchain (`aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc` 17, binutils including `-objdump` and `-windres`).
+- The ARM64 sysroot `C:\msys64\usr\aarch64-pc-cygwin`, which must contain `msys-2.0.dll`, libintl and libiconv.
+- `crossarm64/config.site` from MSYS2-packages, so configure probes run natively.
+
+### Build
+```bash
+MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /c/wos-eval/work/xz && mkdir -p build-arm64 && cd build-arm64 && export lt_cv_deplibs_check_method=pass_all CONFIG_SITE=/home/HCKTest/MSYS2-packages/crossarm64/config.site && MSYSTEM=CYGWIN ../configure --build=x86_64-pc-msys --host=aarch64-pc-cygwin --prefix=/usr --enable-shared --enable-static --without-libintl-prefix --without-libiconv-prefix CPPFLAGS=-I/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/include LDFLAGS=-L/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/lib'
+MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /c/wos-eval/work/xz/build-arm64 && make -j8'
+```
+Build output: `build-arm64/src/liblzma/.libs/msys-lzma-5.dll`, `build-arm64/src/xz/.libs/xz.exe`, `build-arm64/src/xzdec/.libs/{xzdec,lzmadec}.exe`, `build-arm64/src/lzmainfo/.libs/lzmainfo.exe`.
+
+The build runs at the default `-O2`. GCC 17 hit no internal compiler errors. `config.h` has `HAVE_ARM64_CRC32 1` and `TUKLIB_FAST_UNALIGNED_ACCESS 1`. `aarch64-pc-cygwin-objdump -d msys-lzma-5.dll | grep -c 'crc32[bhwx]'` gives 8, and the DLL imports `IsProcessorFeaturePresent`.
+
+The MSYS2 recipe that builds this package (`MSYS2-packages/xz/PKGBUILD`) already has an aarch64 cross arm.
+
+### Run Tests
+The ARM64 runtime DLLs and the uninstalled liblzma must be on `PATH`. Without them every test exits 127, because the DLLs are not found.
+```bash
+MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /c/wos-eval/work/xz/build-arm64 && export PATH="$PATH:/c/wos-eval/work/xz/build-arm64/src/liblzma/.libs:/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin" && make check'
+```
+Expected: 22 passed, 0 failed (90 TAP subtests).
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+xz has no benchmark suite. The ad-hoc scripts live outside the repo in `C:\wos-eval\work\xz-scratch`:
+- `crcbench.c`: `lzma_crc32` over a 256 MiB buffer.
+- `bench.sh`: end-to-end runs, baseline package against this port.
+- `bench2.sh`: unpatched `-O2` control against this port.
+```bash
+cd /c/wos-eval/work/xz-scratch && ./bench.sh && ./bench2.sh
+PATH="$PATH:/c/msys64/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin" ./new/crcbench.exe 7
+```
+Results are in `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`.
+
