+## Benchmark Results
+- **Result file**: `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt` (committed on `arm64-port`)
+- **Metadata**: `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`
+- **Format**: txt
+- **Executed on**: native ARM64 host. Another job's test suite was running at the same time, so the end-to-end numbers are noisy.
+
+| Measurement | Pre-port package (-O0) | Unpatched main, -O2 | arm64-port, -O2 |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `lzma_crc32`, 256 MiB (MiB/s) | 615 | 1681 | 6255 to 7785 |
+| `xz -T1 -6`, 64 MiB (ms, median) | 34783 | n/a | 17992 |
+| `xz -dc`, 64 MiB (ms, median) | 336 | n/a | 252 |
+| `xz -T1 -0 --check=crc32`, 64 MiB (ms, median) | 10140 | 5581 | 6065 (within noise) |
+| `xz -t` on the crc32 file (ms, median) | 1972 | 841 | 890 (within noise) |
+
+Reading the table:
+- The CRC32 change on its own gives a 3.7x faster `lzma_crc32` than generic C at the same `-O2`.
+- The end-to-end gains over the shipped package come mostly from `-O2` against the cross conf's `-O0`, not from the CRC change.
+
+## NEON Optimizations
+Skipped. Phase 7 did not run because `WOS_SKIP_OPTIMIZE` was set. xz has no x86 SIMD translation units that need porting:
+- `crc_x86_clmul.h` and the `memcmplen.h`/`lz_decoder.h` SSE2 paths are guarded and fall back to portable C on aarch64.
+- CRC64 has no ARM64 implementation upstream.
