+## Limitations & Known Issues
+None. All reachable limitations were resolved.
+
+Design facts and notes (these are not unattempted work):
+- CRC64, the default `.xz` check, has no ARM64 hardware path in upstream xz (`crc_common.h`: "CRC64 could be done with CLMUL but it's not implemented yet"). It uses generic slice-by-4 on every aarch64 OS.
+- In this cross build, libtool prints `LT_CYGPATH is empty` while linking the uninstalled wrapper executables. These lines are harmless: the build exits 0 and the tests pass once the ARM64 runtime directory is on `PATH`, as shown above.
+- gettext writes `po/*.gmo`, `po/xz.pot` and `po/stamp-po` into the source tree even for an out-of-tree build. They are generated files and are not committed.
+
+## Reverting / Coexistence
+The x86_64/i686 builds are unchanged: the new code is only reached when `__CYGWIN__` is set and the ARM64 CRC32 path is selected. To build x64, switch back to `main` or configure without `--host=aarch64-pc-cygwin`.
